A||||9||truxpin||Hard Ridin' Fiero !!!||||5||
Z||000000||truxpin||10-10-2001||07:32 PM||||This may seem like an easy question for y'all, but remember I have'nt owned a car in about 8 years( I'm a motorcycle man)<BR>I recently bought an '87 GT, now I knew Fiero's were sports cars, and because of that it was'nt going to ride like a Cadalliac. BUT, this thing rides like 2 axels welded to a frame!  <BR>Every little bump shakes like I've never experienced in a car before. <BR>I figured I'd start out by putting on new shocks & struts to begin with.<BR>My question is this: is it possible that the other components in the suspension(mainly the old rubber bushings) have hardened up and could stand to be replaced?? <BR>When I had the car up on jacks last week to inspect, I put the lift under both pass. & driver side lower arms to see just how much lift they were absorbing. Well I got both to raise up about an inch before they started lifting the entire side of the car. Should'nt there be a little more travel in the suspension before movement of the entire body of the car ??   <BR>Todd.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-10-2001||08:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by truxpin:<BR><B>This may seem like an easy question for y'all, but remember I have'nt owned a car in about 8 years( I'm a motorcycle man)<BR>I recently bought an '87 GT, now I knew Fiero's were sports cars, and because of that it was'nt going to ride like a Cadalliac. BUT, this thing rides like 2 axels welded to a frame!  <BR>Every little bump shakes like I've never experienced in a car before. <BR>I figured I'd start out by putting on new shocks & struts to begin with.<BR>My question is this: is it possible that the other components in the suspension(mainly the old rubber bushings) have hardened up and could stand to be replaced?? <BR>When I had the car up on jacks last week to inspect, I put the lift under both pass. & driver side lower arms to see just how much lift they were absorbing. Well I got both to raise up about an inch before they started lifting the entire side of the car. Should'nt there be a little more travel in the suspension before movement of the entire body of the car ??   <BR>Todd.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Todd!<BR>Depends on any mods the previous owner may have added...<BR>Poly bushings, stiff shocks, 16 inch wheels...<BR>Most people enjoy the stock ride, but there are a few of us that like the stiff, slide around the corner suspention...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||truxpin||10-10-2001||08:41 PM||||I see your point, but that leads me to believe that I definatly have some kind of problem. Wheels are stock 15", and as far as I can tell there have not been any upgrades to suspension. I was unable to read any markings on shocks & struts(I'm guessing they're stock equipment) Actually everything I saw down under looked to be original equipment(my guess anyway) <BR>The car itself handles good(I think) but it takes the bumps(even small ones ) so hard it rattles my teeth! I was hoping when I removed the tires I would see some kind of changes made to suspension, but no dice.||||reg||1
Z||000003||gt boy||10-10-2001||09:21 PM||||stick a whoopie cushion under your seat...well it will help for the first few bumps anyways...plus i will make for a good conversation piece when you take out that special someone! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||10-10-2001||09:25 PM||||I suggest replacing shocks and struts first.  If they're original, you probably need to replace them anyhow.<P>It's also possible that a previous owner lowered the car by cutting the springs.  (As I did.)  That will definitely stiffen the ride.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||10-10-2001||11:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gt boy:<BR><B>stick a whoopie cushion under your seat...well it will help for the first few bumps anyways...plus i will make for a good conversation piece when you take out that special someone!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ROFLMAO! Dude, I'm almost crying cuz I'm laughing so hard! The whoopie cushion was my favorite toy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyway, yes replace shocks, struts. I just replaced my struts a week ago, and the old ones were toast. I could push down the "piston" and it wouldn't go back up. My car rides nicer now. I'll be replacing the shocks tomorrow, so that should help out even more. That should give you a good starting point.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000006||Tigger||10-10-2001||11:28 PM||||Hmmm... if the shocks and struts were worn, the ride would be more "floaty" than harsh.<P>I wouldn't blame it on the bushings getting hard.  I'd have to say it's high rate springs or they've been cut.  Tire pressures ok?||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||10-11-2001||02:30 PM||||welcome to a 'sports or sporty' car. you think Fieros ride harsh, try a Vette, any Vette. 3 hours in a Vette and my butt was so numb, I couldnt feel it anymore.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroRacer||10-11-2001||10:54 PM||||Numb butt?  I thought it did that to massage my butt?||||reg||1
Z||000009||lowCG||10-12-2001||12:12 AM||||Yeah those stock suspensions aren't very refined compared to foreign spoprtscars,or better yet motorcycles.Kind of a cross between old Chevette and older Citation,really.||||reg||1
